            <ArticleTitle>Ether lipids and their elusive function in the nervous system: a role for plasmalogens: An Editorial Highlight for 'Reduced muscle strength in ether lipid-deficient mice is accompanied by altered development and function of the neuromuscular junction' on page 569.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>463-466</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1111/jnc.14156</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>In this editorial, we highlight the recent work of Dorninger et al. that demonstrates a reduction in plasmalogens in the motor end plate is associated with a reduction in motor end plate function. This reduction in function is illuminated in reduced muscle function in these mice, corresponding with the reduction in acetylcholine release and in its receptor density observed in these mice.</AbstractText>
                <CopyrightInformation>© 2017 International Society for Neurochemistry.</CopyrightInformation>
            </Abstract>
